.TH VIBEOS-WAKEUP 8 "2026-11-16" "vibeos 0.1.0" "VibeOS"
.SH NAME
vibeos-wakeup \- wake the phone at the times apps ask for
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vibeos-wakeup
.SH DESCRIPTION
Holds one CLOCK_REALTIME_ALARM timer for all apps, as Android's AlarmManager does for RTC_WAKEUP alarms: at the earliest time any app asked for, the kernel wakes the phone from suspend, and vibeos-wakeup holds it awake for a moment (a logind sleep inhibitor) so the app's own timer fires. It owns vibeos.Wakeup on the system bus, at /vibeos/Wakeup: Set(s name, x time, a{sv} options) sets or (with time 0) removes a wake-up; the option "alarm-clock" (b) marks an alarm the user set, "app" (s) the app that shows it. The read-only property NextAlarmClock (xs) is the earliest alarm clock. Nothing is stored: apps set their wake-ups again when the name appears.
.SH SEE ALSO
busctl(1), systemd-inhibit(1)
